/-!
# Odd models in the rank-one component reduction

The explicit reduced configuration excludes L₃(3) by its semidihedral
Sylow structure and excludes L₂(p), p > 7 a Fermat or Mersenne prime,
by maximality of its Sylow two-subgroups. Actual model comparisons carry
p = 5 and p = 7 to the characteristic-two branches handled by the parent.

For A₇, the moving normal four-group and residual generation identify Y₊
with A₄. The actual seven-point component action also identifies M ∩ I
as the preimage of the stabilizer of a partition of type 2,2,2,1, with
kernel C_I(L). This completes the odd-model exclusions from the explicit
configuration. The parent retains source assembly for Theorem 15.3.43
and the even-model exclusions used by the two small-parameter bridges.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.3.43, printed pp.1139--1140, and 1.1.5(3)(d)--(e), printed pp.501--502.
-/
